WEBVTT


00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:11.901
<i>At first, I didn't believe it either.</i>


00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:14.596
<i>But the gods of Olympus are real.</i>


00:01:14.793 --> 00:01:18.107
<i>And sometimes,
these gods have children with humans...</i>


00:01:18.296 --> 00:01:20.107
<i>called half-bloods.</i>


00:01:20.298 --> 00:01:21.677
<i>I'm one of them.</i>


00:01:21.866 --> 00:01:25.909
<i>I'm Percy Jackson.
Son of Poseidon, god of the sea.</i>


00:01:34.379 --> 00:01:39.733
<i>Seven years ago, four of these children
were headed to Camp Half-Blood...</i>


00:01:39.919 --> 00:01:43.461
<i>the only place on Earth
that is safe for our kind.</i>


00:01:44.424 --> 00:01:46.235
<i>Only three of them made it.</i>


00:01:53.599 --> 00:01:55.103
We're almost at camp!


00:01:59.172 --> 00:02:00.379
Look out!


00:02:02.775 --> 00:02:04.484
Grover! Luke, help him!


00:02:04.677 --> 00:02:05.748
Grover, are you okay?


00:02:05.846 --> 00:02:07.919
My leg. it's stuck.


00:02:12.452 --> 00:02:13.865
Come on. I got you.


00:02:13.954 --> 00:02:15.525
Keep going. I'll hold them off.


00:02:15.621 --> 00:02:18.731
No, Thalia. They'll kill you.


00:02:25.498 --> 00:02:27.743
Go, Luke. I'll be right behind you.


00:02:29.103 --> 00:02:30.743
Over here!


00:02:31.839 --> 00:02:33.319
Annabeth, come on!


00:02:35.943 --> 00:02:37.014
Stay back.


00:02:45.987 --> 00:02:47.296
Thalia, come on!


00:02:50.492 --> 00:02:53.339
No! Thalia!


00:02:57.565 --> 00:03:02.747
<i>He! name was Thalia,
and she gave her life to save three.</i>


00:03:07.575 --> 00:03:11.083
<i>And so, as Thalia lay dying...</i>


00:03:11.279 --> 00:03:15.527
<i>her father Zeus found
another way for her to live.</i>


00:03:28.264 --> 00:03:30.941
<i>A way for all half-bloods to live.</i>


00:03:31.134 --> 00:03:36.988
<i>A gift to ensure no one in Camp Half-Blood
would die the same way.</i>


00:03:38.742 --> 00:03:43.821
<i>The barrier, to protect them from those
who lived for their death.</i>


00:03:45.549 --> 00:03:46.961
Let's go!


00:03:50.754 --> 00:03:55.036
<i>Every day,
the story of Thalia's bra very inspires me.</i>


00:03:56.893 --> 00:04:00.538
<i>And her tree protects my home.</i>


00:04:02.332 --> 00:04:05.213
<i>But not always my head.</i>


00:04:13.644 --> 00:04:16.787
How nice of you to show up
just to watch me win.


00:04:16.981 --> 00:04:19.760
Everything they say about you
is wrong, Clarisse.


00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:22.229
You actually do have a sense of humor.


00:04:30.795 --> 00:04:33.506
- There goes another one.
- Go, Percy!


00:04:34.299 --> 00:04:37.476
Come on, Percy!
I got 50 drachma on you!


00:04:38.503 --> 00:04:39.848
You bet on this?


00:04:40.038 --> 00:04:41.677
What, is that wrong?


00:04:46.945 --> 00:04:49.689
'97 Xinomavro. Would you like a taste?


00:04:49.881 --> 00:04:53.457
Why do you torture yourself, Dionysus?


00:04:56.387 --> 00:04:58.335
It was one transgression, one.


00:04:58.523 --> 00:05:01.006
And with a naiad,
for the sake of Olympus.


00:05:01.192 --> 00:05:03.197
How was I to know that
Zeus had a thing for her?


00:05:03.295 --> 00:05:06.610
Or that he could
hold a grudge for so long?


00:05:11.838 --> 00:05:13.547
I think the fact
that Zeus is immortal...


00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:16.783
means there's no limit
to how long he can hold a grudge.


00:05:16.976 --> 00:05:19.892
The Christians have a guy
who can do this trick in reverse.


00:05:19.979 --> 00:05:21.619
Now, that's a god.


00:05:24.651 --> 00:05:27.099
Aren't you tired of getting beat,
Jackson?


00:05:44.404 --> 00:05:46.682
Clarissa!


00:05:51.278 --> 00:05:53.089
Help! Help me!


00:06:08.763 --> 00:06:10.437
Tereus, grab my hand!


00:06:11.165 --> 00:06:13.078
Good luck with that.


00:06:14.568 --> 00:06:15.640
'90! you.


00:06:23.277 --> 00:06:24.450
Thank you!


00:06:25.814 --> 00:06:26.793
Percy!


00:06:37.659 --> 00:06:40.438
Clarissa! Clarissa! Clarissa!


00:06:47.637 --> 00:06:50.780
So, what I'm wondering is, Percy...


00:06:50.973 --> 00:06:54.925
that first quest you went on,
beginner's luck, wasn't it?


00:06:55.678 --> 00:06:59.630
Clarisse, he saved Olympus.
That's more than you've ever done.


00:07:01.784 --> 00:07:02.855
Whatever.


00:07:03.053 --> 00:07:05.228
Even for the daughter of the god of war,
that girl's a mythic bi--


00:07:05.321 --> 00:07:06.528
Don't listen to her, Percy.


00:07:06.622 --> 00:07:08.331
You know, it's too late.


00:07:08.524 --> 00:07:10.699
Besides, she has a point.


00:07:10.894 --> 00:07:12.465
Dude, what are you talking about?


00:07:12.562 --> 00:07:14.635
You're more than a one-quest wonder.


00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:16.804
You recovered Ares' stolen chariot.


00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:19.178
No, actually, that was Clarissa.


00:07:19.369 --> 00:07:22.649
Okay, what about the Fall Tournament?
You owned that sucker.


00:07:22.806 --> 00:07:23.808
Clarissa?


00:07:24.975 --> 00:07:27.857
Okay, the Solstice Games?
The Bronze Dragon's Quest?


00:07:32.382 --> 00:07:34.797
Thank you for trying to cheer me up.


00:07:35.318 --> 00:07:36.731
I would lick a pair of cloven hooves...


00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:38.769
before I let you listen to Clarisse
instead of us.


00:07:38.856 --> 00:07:39.858
No offense, Grover.


00:07:39.957 --> 00:07:41.768
None taken. Is that an offer?


00:07:41.859 --> 00:07:44.171
Listen, it doesn't matter
what Clarissa has done.


00:07:44.261 --> 00:07:46.642
To Chiron and Mr. D,
you're still the rock star.


00:07:46.731 --> 00:07:48.474
Perry Johnson!


00:07:48.933 --> 00:07:51.040
Actually, it's Percy Jackson, sir.


00:07:51.235 --> 00:07:52.214
Whatever.


00:07:52.404 --> 00:07:55.046
I have a very important task
to entrust you with.


00:07:55.139 --> 00:07:56.175
You do?


00:07:56.274 --> 00:07:59.258
Yes, it's a critical assignment.
And it's very taxing.


00:07:59.344 --> 00:08:00.585
Can I trust you?


00:08:00.678 --> 00:08:01.680
Of course.


00:08:01.779 --> 00:08:03.818
Good. You'll need this.


00:08:06.083 --> 00:08:10.332
Sometimes these events
get a little messy.


00:08:19.164 --> 00:08:20.872
<i>Maybe Clarissa was right.</i>


00:08:23.401 --> 00:08:25.747
Maybe I only stopped
Luke from destroying Olympus...


00:08:25.837 --> 00:08:28.880
because I had Annabeth and Grover
helping me, right?


00:08:31.644 --> 00:08:32.989
Dad?


00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:35.923
Poseidon?


00:08:43.489 --> 00:08:48.341
Have you ever felt like everything
you've ever done...


00:08:48.527 --> 00:08:50.509
maybe you didn't really do it?


00:08:51.665 --> 00:08:53.806
It was all just luck or something?


00:08:56.603 --> 00:08:58.607
No, of course not.


00:08:58.805 --> 00:09:00.308
You're a god.


00:09:01.941 --> 00:09:06.588
Speaking as someone who's not,
it sucks.


00:09:09.182 --> 00:09:12.827
It makes you question whether
you were all that good to begin with.


00:09:17.991 --> 00:09:22.001
Okay. Good not talking to you.


00:09:22.630 --> 00:09:23.666
Again.


00:09:34.875 --> 00:09:36.322
So, he just walked right in?


00:09:36.411 --> 00:09:38.324
He just walked straight into camp?


00:09:38.413 --> 00:09:40.395
It seems he lumbered, actually.


00:09:40.581 --> 00:09:42.563
I don't care if he sashayed!


00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:46.292
What's the point of having this mystical
protective barrier if any thing can just--


00:09:46.387 --> 00:09:49.200
Could you not touch that, please?
That's a very precious Grenache.


00:09:49.290 --> 00:09:50.292
I think the point is...


00:09:50.391 --> 00:09:53.500
since he did pass right through
the barrier from Thalia's tree...


00:09:53.594 --> 00:09:57.136
- Don't say it.
-...It means he's most likely a god-spawn.


00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:01.913
Yeah, but the spawn of which god?


00:10:02.103 --> 00:10:03.812
I know.


00:10:07.843 --> 00:10:09.380
Poseidon.


00:10:22.058 --> 00:10:24.769
So, why did Mr. D summon you?
It's not good to get summoned.


00:10:24.861 --> 00:10:25.932
I'm sure it's fine.


00:10:26.028 --> 00:10:27.064
I'm sure you don't get summoned


00:10:27.163 --> 00:10:29.042
to the Big House
without a major-league screw-up.


00:10:29.131 --> 00:10:30.305
I didn't screw up.


00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:32.814
I cleaned the entire coliseum.
And vacuumed.


00:10:32.902 --> 00:10:34.884
Don't let him get into your head, okay?


00:10:34.971 --> 00:10:37.853
We have a dead camper walking.
Dead camper walking, here.


00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:39.751
Thanks. This is friendship.


00:10:39.942 --> 00:10:41.787
I'm just playing,
just trying to have a little fun.


00:10:41.878 --> 00:10:43.120
It's all right.


00:10:43.313 --> 00:10:45.352
So, it's okay if I get your cabin
when you get kicked out?


00:10:45.448 --> 00:10:47.828
Seriously, don't worry. it's just Mr. D.


00:10:47.917 --> 00:10:51.095
I mean, if Chiron had summoned you,
then...


00:10:55.625 --> 00:10:57.904
You are so massively screwed.


00:10:59.662 --> 00:11:02.646
Whatever it is you think I did,
I didn't do it.


00:11:02.833 --> 00:11:04.337
You've done nothing, Percy.


00:11:04.435 --> 00:11:05.608
Exactly.


00:11:05.804 --> 00:11:10.223
As you know,
you are believed to be Poseidon's only heir.


00:11:10.909 --> 00:11:12.116
Yeah, so?


00:11:12.310 --> 00:11:16.421
So, it would seem that belief
has been held in error.


00:11:16.681 --> 00:11:18.685
Hold on.
You're saying Percy has a brother?


00:11:18.783 --> 00:11:20.286
Or a sister.


00:11:23.021 --> 00:11:26.096
Holy Styx. Another Poseidon half-blood.


00:11:27.492 --> 00:11:28.904
Not exactly.


00:11:30.094 --> 00:11:32.600
Technically, Tyson is not a half-blood.


00:11:32.797 --> 00:11:35.040
Half-bloods are half-human,
hence the name.


00:11:35.133 --> 00:11:36.340
I don't get it.


00:11:36.435 --> 00:11:39.749
If this new kid is not half-human,
then what other half is he?


00:11:39.838 --> 00:11:42.013
Nymph. Sea nymph.


00:11:42.206 --> 00:11:44.382
And when you cross a deity with a nymph,
you get...


00:11:44.476 --> 00:11:47.084
Don't touch. it's a Gewurztraminer.


00:11:47.279 --> 00:11:48.520
Hi.


00:11:50.114 --> 00:11:51.618
Hi, Brother.


00:12:13.039 --> 00:12:16.285
So, you're the big shot here, right?
You saved the world and stuff.


00:12:16.376 --> 00:12:18.483
Yeah. Yeah.


00:12:20.313 --> 00:12:22.488
Hey. they put peppers in yours.


00:12:22.983 --> 00:12:24.622
Are you gonna eat that?


00:12:25.618 --> 00:12:27.031
Go ahead.


00:12:30.991 --> 00:12:32.768
Is he messing with me?


00:12:32.959 --> 00:12:34.234
I think he's hungry.


00:12:34.327 --> 00:12:36.366
No, not him. I meant Poseidon.


00:12:36.562 --> 00:12:38.441
Is this supposed to be
some kind of joke?


00:12:38.531 --> 00:12:41.812
A half-brother? A Cyclops? Come on.


00:12:43.704 --> 00:12:46.951
I think the politically correct term
is "ocularly impaired."


00:12:47.141 --> 00:12:48.622
And a half-brother
is better than nothing.


00:12:48.710 --> 00:12:50.122
I like having a brother.


00:12:50.211 --> 00:12:51.817
Dad was cool to bring me here.


00:12:51.913 --> 00:12:53.622
Dad? Dad brought you here?


00:12:54.482 --> 00:12:56.292
I was upstate, in the woods.


00:12:56.384 --> 00:13:00.564
One day, this trident shows up over
my head, and then it started moving south.


00:13:00.655 --> 00:13:04.196
And you followed it.
You followed it here.


00:13:04.759 --> 00:13:06.171
It glowed.


00:13:06.361 --> 00:13:09.402
Well, somebody has got a new brother.


00:13:10.031 --> 00:13:12.810
And I can see he's got his daddy's eyes.


00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:13.979
Well...


00:13:14.702 --> 00:13:15.681
"Eye."


00:13:17.004 --> 00:13:19.613
You should really get him
some sprayable mist.


00:13:19.774 --> 00:13:23.419
Anyway, it is kind of interesting timing,
don't you think?


00:13:23.611 --> 00:13:28.531
Maybe Poseidon decided he needed
another son to, you know...


00:13:28.716 --> 00:13:29.821
represent.


00:13:30.018 --> 00:13:31.362
Bull.


00:13:31.753 --> 00:13:32.995
Excuse me?


00:13:33.188 --> 00:13:34.532
Smells like bull.


00:13:45.134 --> 00:13:46.706
We got barrier action.


00:13:48.437 --> 00:13:50.043
Hey, Chris, you coming?


00:13:50.239 --> 00:13:52.414
No, I'm good.


00:14:03.252 --> 00:14:04.892
That is so awesome.


00:14:06.890 --> 00:14:09.635
It's chill. The barrier is holding.


00:14:18.668 --> 00:14:19.807
A Colchis bull.


00:14:19.903 --> 00:14:21.110
Run!


00:14:34.185 --> 00:14:35.164
Percy!


00:14:36.321 --> 00:14:37.323
Come on!


00:15:05.116 --> 00:15:07.029
- We have to find its weak spot.
- Does it have one?


00:15:07.118 --> 00:15:09.122
Percy, distract it for me.


00:15:50.730 --> 00:15:52.336
I got this.


00:16:35.644 --> 00:16:36.646
Bad bull.


00:16:38.580 --> 00:16:39.924
Hey, rust bucket!


00:17:59.196 --> 00:18:01.235
Damn it, Jackson.


00:18:03.735 --> 00:18:08.246
Do you have any idea
how hard Colchis bulls are to come by?


00:18:09.374 --> 00:18:11.879
Maybe next time
you try to drown someone...


00:18:13.010 --> 00:18:17.862
you'll first make sure he's not
a demigod who can swim.


00:18:23.221 --> 00:18:24.292
Luke?


00:18:24.389 --> 00:18:27.896
Turns out, you're not the only
half-blood who's hard to kill.


00:18:30.595 --> 00:18:32.668
You know, prophecy.


00:18:34.299 --> 00:18:36.942
What prophecy?
What are you talking about?


00:18:37.135 --> 00:18:38.615
You don't know?


00:18:39.404 --> 00:18:40.406
Huh.


00:18:41.073 --> 00:18:45.457
Add that to the long list of things
your buddy Chiron hasn't shared with you.


00:18:46.444 --> 00:18:49.588
Chiron, Mr. D, all the rest...


00:18:50.583 --> 00:18:52.725
they don't care about us.


00:18:53.252 --> 00:18:56.031
To them, we're just kids.


00:18:56.222 --> 00:18:59.502
A bunch of pawns meant to be
pushed around, told what to do.


00:18:59.893 --> 00:19:02.341
I'm not the only half-blood
who thinks so.


00:19:05.298 --> 00:19:06.540
Think about it.


00:19:20.079 --> 00:19:21.321
What did I miss?


00:19:21.415 --> 00:19:22.622
Where's Percy?


00:19:22.716 --> 00:19:25.825
Last time I saw him,
he was getting dragged by a Colchis bull.


00:19:25.919 --> 00:19:27.798
Hey, you.


00:19:28.222 --> 00:19:29.566
How come you aren't barbecued?


00:19:29.656 --> 00:19:31.228
Cyclopes are fireproof.


00:19:31.325 --> 00:19:33.773
How did the bull get through the barrier?


00:19:35.262 --> 00:19:37.073
Oh, my gods.


00:19:59.921 --> 00:20:01.230
Poisoned.


00:20:01.422 --> 00:20:03.335
Is she... ls the tree dead?


00:20:03.524 --> 00:20:05.096
No, but dying.


00:20:08.396 --> 00:20:11.505
A condition we're about to become
all too familiar with.


00:20:12.033 --> 00:20:16.008
Everybody, we're going to need
a guard detail to patrol the perimeter.


00:20:16.204 --> 00:20:19.086
It feels like she's dying all over again.


00:20:20.208 --> 00:20:22.247
Who would do this?


00:20:23.278 --> 00:20:24.987
Luke poisoned the tree.


00:20:25.847 --> 00:20:27.088
Percy!


00:20:27.449 --> 00:20:29.225
Yay, you're alive.


00:20:29.951 --> 00:20:32.161
Yeah, I'm not the only one.


00:20:32.789 --> 00:20:34.269
Luke let the bull in.


00:20:34.457 --> 00:20:35.869
Without the tree's barrier...


00:20:35.958 --> 00:20:37.769
he probably figures there's enough


00:20:37.860 --> 00:20:39.535
demi-Titans out there
to get him what he wants.


00:20:39.629 --> 00:20:41.838
And that would be what, exactly?


00:20:42.532 --> 00:20:45.243
Our annihilation, Ms. La Rue.


00:20:45.735 --> 00:20:47.876
Our annihilation.


00:20:56.113 --> 00:20:57.491
How's the antidote coming?


00:20:57.580 --> 00:20:58.855
Slowly.


00:21:00.217 --> 00:21:02.699
I know this probably isn't the best time...


00:21:05.055 --> 00:21:06.501
but there's something I have to ask you.


00:21:06.589 --> 00:21:07.934
What is it?


00:21:09.927 --> 00:21:12.535
It was something Luke said
about a prophecy...


00:21:12.729 --> 00:21:14.711
how I'm mentioned in it.


00:21:15.498 --> 00:21:17.571
Do you know anything about this?


00:21:19.436 --> 00:21:22.113
Knowledge isn't always power, Percy.


00:21:22.906 --> 00:21:24.911
Sometimes, it's a burden.


00:21:25.576 --> 00:21:27.114
I know that.


00:21:28.112 --> 00:21:30.748
But like you said,
I've been pretty unexceptional lately.


00:21:30.749 --> 00:21:31.159
But like you said,
I've been pretty unexceptional lately.


00:21:31.249 --> 00:21:35.360
It's got me wondering
if I'm prophecy-worthy.


00:21:35.554 --> 00:21:37.866
They say that when the gods
wish to torture us...


00:21:37.956 --> 00:21:39.733
they answer our prayers.


00:21:39.924 --> 00:21:43.535
Necklace of Harmonia, Hercules' bow,
Golden Apple of Discord.


00:21:43.962 --> 00:21:45.534
Three millennia of gods and demigods...


00:21:45.630 --> 00:21:48.705
you'd think that someone would have
come up with a cure for Thalia's tree.


00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:52.479
Persephone did come up with Miracle-Gro.
Maybe we can try that.


00:21:52.671 --> 00:21:53.946
That's it.


00:21:55.173 --> 00:21:56.483
Right here.


00:21:57.809 --> 00:22:01.021
That is not gonna cure Thalia's tree
so much as get us all killed.


00:22:01.112 --> 00:22:02.320
Me, in particular.


00:22:02.414 --> 00:22:05.261
It's perfect. it's exactly what we need.


00:22:06.751 --> 00:22:08.232
I'm taking this to Mr. D.


00:22:08.320 --> 00:22:09.391
No.


00:22:15.261 --> 00:22:19.042
I was hoping to spare you this onus
a little while longer, but go inside.


00:22:19.132 --> 00:22:20.612
Upstairs, to the attic.


00:22:20.700 --> 00:22:23.206
And when you come back down,
we'll talk some more.


00:22:23.303 --> 00:22:26.014
Assuming you're still sane, that is.


00:22:59.039 --> 00:23:01.454
I am the spirit of Delphi...


00:23:01.642 --> 00:23:04.489
speaker of the prophecies
of Phoebus Apollo...


00:23:04.678 --> 00:23:06.957
slayer of the mighty Python.


00:23:07.148 --> 00:23:10.793
Approach, seeker, and ask.


00:23:13.187 --> 00:23:15.602
I heard there was a prophecy about me.


00:23:15.790 --> 00:23:17.169
Aye.


00:23:17.359 --> 00:23:22.143
But before you learn the future,
know first the past.


00:23:24.065 --> 00:23:27.482
<i>Long ago, before our time...</i>


00:23:27.669 --> 00:23:29.708
<i>before Olympus and the gods...</i>


00:23:29.904 --> 00:23:33.185
<i>Titans ruled the world.</i>


00:23:33.741 --> 00:23:35.450
<i>Led by Kronos...</i>


00:23:35.643 --> 00:23:40.063
<i>a force so evil,
he devoured his own children.</i>


00:23:40.248 --> 00:23:42.730
<i>But three of his sons escaped.</i>


00:23:42.918 --> 00:23:46.198
<i>Zeus, Hades and Poseidon.</i>


00:23:51.193 --> 00:23:52.799
<i>They destroyed Kronos...</i>


00:23:52.895 --> 00:23:57.473
<i>and banished his remains
to the depths of Tartarus.</i>


00:23:58.234 --> 00:24:02.380
<i>But Kronos is fated to rise again...</i>


00:24:02.572 --> 00:24:07.286
<i>to exact his vengeance on Olympus,
and the world.</i>


00:24:09.112 --> 00:24:14.396
<i>Only one half-blood child of the
three eldest gods can defeat him.</i>


00:24:14.584 --> 00:24:17.796
<i>This child shall be our salvation...</i>


00:24:17.987 --> 00:24:21.130
<i>or the cause of our destruction.</i>


00:24:23.893 --> 00:24:28.369
<i>It all begins when two cousins
grapple for a fleece...</i>


00:24:28.798 --> 00:24:31.782
<i>the son of the sea
and the lightning thief.</i>


00:24:32.636 --> 00:24:33.707
Luke.


00:24:33.903 --> 00:24:36.409
And that half-blood
of the eldest gods...


00:24:36.606 --> 00:24:39.556
shall reach 20 against all odds.


00:24:39.743 --> 00:24:42.989
"And see the world in endless sleep...


00:24:43.180 --> 00:24:46.960
"the evil soul,
cursed blade shall reap.


00:24:47.151 --> 00:24:48.996
"A single choice shall end his days...


00:24:49.086 --> 00:24:52.469
"Olympus to preserve or raze."


00:24:52.657 --> 00:24:56.108
And that is "raze" with a
as in "destroy."


00:24:56.627 --> 00:24:58.108
l asked.


00:25:00.598 --> 00:25:04.482
Is there any chance,
any chance at all...


00:25:04.669 --> 00:25:07.916
that I might not be the guy
in the prophecy?


00:25:08.106 --> 00:25:10.953
The Oracle references
a half-blood of the eldest gods.


00:25:11.042 --> 00:25:16.156
You are the only living half-blood heir
of Zeus, Hades or Poseidon.


00:25:16.347 --> 00:25:18.660
The prophecy could refer only to you.


00:25:18.850 --> 00:25:22.426
What if I destroy Olympus...


00:25:22.621 --> 00:25:25.764
by not being good enough to save it?


00:25:26.858 --> 00:25:29.306
That seems to be the question,
doesn't it?


00:25:30.796 --> 00:25:32.037
It's absolutely out of the question.


00:25:32.130 --> 00:25:34.112
If you could just listen to me
for one moment--


00:25:34.199 --> 00:25:36.147
lam listening.
You want to go on a quest.


00:25:36.234 --> 00:25:37.544
It must be Thursday.


00:25:37.636 --> 00:25:40.779
I'm serious.
I'm absolutely sure that this is gonna work.


00:25:42.875 --> 00:25:44.550
It was such a good year.


00:25:44.744 --> 00:25:47.353
The Golden Fleece
can heal any living person or thing...


00:25:47.447 --> 00:25:49.759
including Thalia's tree.


00:25:49.949 --> 00:25:53.092
We heal the tree,
we restore the barrier around camp.


00:25:54.053 --> 00:25:56.468
I'm surprised you want to go along
with her on this, Mr. Undershirt.


00:25:56.556 --> 00:25:57.535
Underwood.


00:25:57.624 --> 00:25:58.763
Whatever.


00:25:59.192 --> 00:26:02.608
Every satyr who has ever
gone after the Fleece has died.


00:26:02.795 --> 00:26:05.278
Right? I mentioned that to her.


00:26:06.099 --> 00:26:09.915
But it's a risk I'm willing to take
for the good of the camp.


00:26:10.603 --> 00:26:12.916
Look, the last I heard...


00:26:13.106 --> 00:26:15.782
the Golden Fleece
was in the Sea of Monsters...


00:26:15.876 --> 00:26:17.949
what the humans call
the Bermuda Triangle.


00:26:18.045 --> 00:26:20.459
A place not only a satyr
should be afraid of.


00:26:20.547 --> 00:26:24.294
So, the answer is no. No.
I'm sorry, Annabelle.


00:26:24.417 --> 00:26:25.396
Annabeth.


00:26:25.485 --> 00:26:28.560
Whatever. it's a terrible idea.


00:26:28.756 --> 00:26:31.204
I've had a grand idea.


00:26:33.061 --> 00:26:35.475
Unless Thalia's tree can be cured...


00:26:35.664 --> 00:26:39.810
and the protective barrier
around our camp restored...


00:26:40.001 --> 00:26:43.646
then every demigod, centaur,
satyr and nymph...


00:26:44.172 --> 00:26:46.553
will be killed within days,
if not sooner.


00:26:46.642 --> 00:26:48.316
Hey, you okay?


00:26:48.977 --> 00:26:51.460
Don't worry, camp will be okay.


00:26:52.080 --> 00:26:53.925
You have to have faith, right?


00:26:54.015 --> 00:26:56.624
But fortunately,
I have considered the matter.


00:26:57.419 --> 00:26:58.398
And after great study...


00:26:58.487 --> 00:27:01.835
I have determined that the only thing
that has the power to save Thalia's tree...


00:27:01.923 --> 00:27:03.632
and therefore our home...


00:27:03.758 --> 00:27:05.762
is the Golden Fleece of myth...


00:27:08.163 --> 00:27:09.302
What?


00:27:09.998 --> 00:27:11.274
...whose touch...


00:27:14.336 --> 00:27:17.320
...can heal every person
and every thing.


00:27:18.873 --> 00:27:22.916
So, a quest, a mission of mercy,
if you will...


00:27:23.112 --> 00:27:25.527
into uncharted and deadly waters...


00:27:25.916 --> 00:27:28.957
with nothing less at stake
than our own survival.


00:27:29.586 --> 00:27:35.235
Now, a satyr is naturally drawn,
as you know, to the power of the Fleece.


00:27:35.425 --> 00:27:39.502
And therefore, it must be a satyr
who will guide a half-blood on this quest.


00:27:39.863 --> 00:27:41.343
Thanks a lot.


00:27:41.998 --> 00:27:43.069
Ichneutae!


00:27:43.667 --> 00:27:45.671
Will you guide the champion?


00:27:45.869 --> 00:27:47.543
Oh, yeah.


00:27:47.738 --> 00:27:50.550
Good. Great! That's great!


00:27:51.942 --> 00:27:52.921
Yeah!


00:27:55.912 --> 00:28:00.923
As to who that champion might be,
our plight calls for only our finest hero.


00:28:01.585 --> 00:28:05.833
The best of us,
the strongest and the bravest.


00:28:06.022 --> 00:28:09.496
The scion of the god of war...


00:28:09.693 --> 00:28:10.695
Clarissa!


00:28:11.329 --> 00:28:12.308
Yes!


00:28:16.066 --> 00:28:17.138
Thank you.


00:28:18.770 --> 00:28:20.445
Her name, he gets right.


00:28:25.076 --> 00:28:27.184
Hey, Clarissa. Clarissa!


00:28:27.379 --> 00:28:28.358
What?


00:28:29.181 --> 00:28:31.595
Don't worry about always
coming in second, Jackson.


00:28:31.683 --> 00:28:33.255
You do get used to it.


00:28:33.351 --> 00:28:35.355
I think, right?
Obviously, I wouldn't know.


00:28:35.454 --> 00:28:36.661
Listen, Luke is still out there.


00:28:36.754 --> 00:28:39.135
He's involved with the Fleece somehow...


00:28:39.457 --> 00:28:41.997
and I've got a feeling
that he's not done yet.


00:28:42.094 --> 00:28:43.073
Really?


00:28:43.228 --> 00:28:45.939
Because I've got a feeling
that I don't really care.


00:28:46.031 --> 00:28:47.842
Gosh, don't look so wounded.


00:28:49.067 --> 00:28:51.345
Listen, there are generals,
and there are foot soldiers.


00:28:51.436 --> 00:28:54.613
And you should feel lucky that you even
made it into the army at all.


00:28:54.706 --> 00:28:58.248
Just try not to screw up anything
too badly while I'm gone. Okay?


00:28:59.444 --> 00:29:00.344
Let's go.


00:29:00.345 --> 00:29:00.447
Let's go.


00:29:10.256 --> 00:29:12.933
"Cursed blade shall reap."


00:29:14.561 --> 00:29:16.634
"Cursed blade shall reap."


00:29:17.964 --> 00:29:21.745
What good is a prophecy
if you can't even understand it?


00:29:25.071 --> 00:29:27.918
I guess you don't have
any answers either, Dad.


00:29:29.409 --> 00:29:31.048
This was your sword.


00:29:43.423 --> 00:29:44.402
This is a bad idea.


00:29:44.491 --> 00:29:45.766
You don't even know
what I was gonna say.


00:29:45.859 --> 00:29:48.365
You were going to say that you're
going after the Fleece to save the camp.


00:29:48.462 --> 00:29:50.944
Actually, he was gonna say "we" were.


00:29:52.133 --> 00:29:54.308
Look, I get what you're doing here.


00:29:54.501 --> 00:29:56.039
You're worried about
the one-quest wonder thing...


00:29:56.136 --> 00:29:57.844
and you want to make your bones.


00:29:57.938 --> 00:30:00.080
But lchneutae and Clarisse
are already going after the Fleece...


00:30:00.175 --> 00:30:02.555
and it's not cool to bogart
on someone else's quest.


00:30:02.643 --> 00:30:04.420
I think this is my quest, too.


00:30:04.512 --> 00:30:06.289
The Oracle says
he wrestles Luke for the Fleece.


00:30:06.381 --> 00:30:09.661
"Grapples." But she also said...


00:30:10.718 --> 00:30:13.828
that I'm destined to destroy Olympus,
or save it.


00:30:17.025 --> 00:30:19.303
Saving is better, obviously.


00:30:19.494 --> 00:30:20.907
Yeah.


00:30:21.830 --> 00:30:25.280
Let me pack a bag and make sure
my health insurance is paid up.


00:30:41.049 --> 00:30:43.031
How are we gonna get past them?


00:30:43.218 --> 00:30:45.131
I think they're looking
for threats trying to come in...


00:30:45.220 --> 00:30:47.601
not people trying to sneak out...


00:30:47.789 --> 00:30:50.500
so, I think we're cool
as long as we stay quiet.


00:30:52.829 --> 00:30:53.808
Sorry!


00:30:58.168 --> 00:30:59.307
We're...


00:31:00.570 --> 00:31:02.176
We're guarding, too.


00:31:03.573 --> 00:31:04.644
You left without me.


00:31:04.741 --> 00:31:07.486
Tyson, where we're going,
it's very dangerous.


00:31:07.677 --> 00:31:09.056
I know. I'm not stupid.


00:31:09.146 --> 00:31:10.455
No,just dumb.


00:31:10.747 --> 00:31:12.057
I want to help.


00:31:13.550 --> 00:31:14.997
You'd do it for me.


00:31:15.185 --> 00:31:16.688
I appreciate that...


00:31:16.887 --> 00:31:20.736
but I don't think you understand
exactly how dangerous this is going to be.


00:31:20.824 --> 00:31:21.963
I do.


00:31:22.159 --> 00:31:24.334
The Fleece is guarded by Polyphemus.


00:31:24.627 --> 00:31:25.606
Who?


00:31:25.695 --> 00:31:26.835
Polyphemus.


00:31:27.031 --> 00:31:29.673
Closest thing Cyclopes
have got to someone famous.


00:31:29.767 --> 00:31:33.047
Captured Odysseus. Lives in Circeland.


00:31:33.237 --> 00:31:34.718
Wait, Circeland?


00:31:34.905 --> 00:31:36.317
Built on his island.


00:31:36.406 --> 00:31:37.819
Long story.


00:31:38.008 --> 00:31:40.183
Point is, maybe I can talk to him.


00:31:40.377 --> 00:31:42.359
You know, Cyclops to Cyclops.


00:31:42.546 --> 00:31:45.428
No, you can't,
because I'm not going with a Cyclops.


00:31:46.951 --> 00:31:50.094
Then we got a problem,
because I'm not going without one.


00:31:50.421 --> 00:31:54.636
This Polyphemus is probably what killed
every satyr that's gone near the Fleece.


00:31:54.726 --> 00:31:56.674
You want me to lead you to a Cyclops?
Fine.


00:31:56.761 --> 00:32:00.041
But I'm bringing along one of my own,
for protection.


00:32:00.732 --> 00:32:01.939
No way.


00:32:02.634 --> 00:32:03.613
No.


00:32:11.376 --> 00:32:13.324
What do you think's
gonna attract more attention...


00:32:13.412 --> 00:32:14.949
all the noise or the one eye?


00:32:15.046 --> 00:32:17.028
Just give the guy a break, okay?


00:32:18.650 --> 00:32:19.721
Okay, fine.


00:32:19.818 --> 00:32:20.820
Keep it down.


00:32:20.919 --> 00:32:23.129
This is crazy hard to come by...


00:32:23.322 --> 00:32:25.304
and I only brought it along
in case of an emergency...


00:32:25.390 --> 00:32:29.638
which I guess this is an emergency,
so... here.


00:32:32.231 --> 00:32:33.267
Mist?


00:32:33.465 --> 00:32:35.505
It makes the mystical look normal.


00:32:35.602 --> 00:32:37.242
"Side effects may include handsomeness,


00:32:37.337 --> 00:32:39.717
headache, self-esteem
and low self-esteem."


00:32:39.806 --> 00:32:41.718
And just know
that if the camp wasn't in danger...


00:32:41.809 --> 00:32:43.153
I wouldn't be wasting this on you.


00:32:43.243 --> 00:32:44.621
Wasting what?


00:32:46.747 --> 00:32:50.095
It's not gonna last forever.
You're gonna have to reapply it.


00:32:58.925 --> 00:33:00.531
Extreme makeover alert.


00:33:04.064 --> 00:33:05.373
How do I look?


00:33:06.567 --> 00:33:09.106
A bit like Dad, actually.


00:33:09.302 --> 00:33:11.284
He's still a Cyclops.


00:33:12.706 --> 00:33:16.179
Grover, where are we going?
What does your nose say?


00:33:17.077 --> 00:33:19.788
Somewhere off the coast of Florida.
South.


00:33:21.882 --> 00:33:23.021
Over here.


00:33:23.217 --> 00:33:24.663
Annie! Hey!


00:33:38.633 --> 00:33:40.706
It's the Chariot of Damnation.


00:33:40.902 --> 00:33:43.010
Looks like a New York City cab.


00:33:43.205 --> 00:33:44.549
Same difference.


00:33:46.674 --> 00:33:49.556
No dollars, no credit cards.
Drachmas only.


00:33:49.744 --> 00:33:51.521
Exact... Change... Please.


00:33:51.713 --> 00:33:53.353
Chop, chop! Get in the cab.


00:33:53.448 --> 00:33:56.330
We just had this cab sanitized
for your protection.


00:33:56.518 --> 00:33:57.828
It wasn't this year, though.


00:33:57.920 --> 00:34:00.368
Excuse me,
we're trying to get to Florida.


00:34:00.723 --> 00:34:03.171
Our kind of fare. Pricey.


00:34:08.063 --> 00:34:10.842
<i>Hey, there.
This is Ganymede, cupbearer to Zeus.</i>


00:34:11.033 --> 00:34:13.379
<i>And when I'm out buying wine
for the lord of the skies...</i>


00:34:13.468 --> 00:34:15.347
<i>I always remember to buckle up.</i>


00:34:15.437 --> 00:34:17.716
Maybe we should have flown commercial.


00:34:20.143 --> 00:34:21.214
Look out!


00:34:24.314 --> 00:34:26.490
Calm down.
If we didn't know what we were doing...


00:34:26.583 --> 00:34:28.222
We wouldn't be licensed.


00:34:31.154 --> 00:34:32.658
They don't have eyes.


00:34:33.657 --> 00:34:34.898
Yeah.


00:34:36.526 --> 00:34:38.599
- I know, awful picture.
- Bad hair day.


00:34:38.695 --> 00:34:40.039
We do so have an eye.


00:34:40.129 --> 00:34:41.804
It's around here somewhere.


00:34:41.898 --> 00:34:44.541
The last time I saw it, you put it
in the glove compartment, Anger.


00:34:44.668 --> 00:34:46.080
Don't use that tone with my name.


00:34:46.170 --> 00:34:47.946
It's not there this time.


00:34:50.341 --> 00:34:52.653
Wasp always puts it with the keys.


00:34:53.310 --> 00:34:56.021
- And it's 20,120.
-So is mine!


00:34:56.213 --> 00:34:58.286
Shouldn't the driver get the eye?


00:34:59.283 --> 00:35:01.026
She'll be fine.


00:35:05.289 --> 00:35:06.667
Tempest, split!


00:35:12.630 --> 00:35:13.609
Percy!


00:35:16.501 --> 00:35:18.414
We paid extra for that option.


00:35:23.008 --> 00:35:25.617
The kid is right.
The driver should have the eyeball.


00:35:25.711 --> 00:35:26.918
He's a freaking genius!


00:35:27.012 --> 00:35:28.458
You're the one that put it in the visor.


00:35:28.546 --> 00:35:32.088
While it's on the table,
I haven't had a turn in quite some time.


00:35:33.218 --> 00:35:34.961
Oh, no, you didn't!


00:35:35.153 --> 00:35:36.292
Yes, I did.


00:35:39.390 --> 00:35:40.962
Hands on the wheel at least, okay?


00:35:45.030 --> 00:35:46.477
- We're all gonna die!
- Pipe down.


00:35:46.565 --> 00:35:49.913
Didn't that prophecy say
you're gonna make it till at least 20?


00:35:50.002 --> 00:35:51.073
You know about the prophecy?


00:35:51.169 --> 00:35:52.912
- Sure.
- The Oracle is a friend.


00:35:53.005 --> 00:35:54.850
- We're besties.
- B-F-F!


00:35:56.475 --> 00:35:57.682
EVE! Eye! Eye!


00:35:57.876 --> 00:35:59.755
Gross! Get it off me!


00:36:02.749 --> 00:36:04.924
What do you know about the prophecy?


00:36:06.920 --> 00:36:07.899
No!


00:36:11.225 --> 00:36:12.330
Okay, okay.


00:36:13.627 --> 00:36:19.379
30. 31, 75,12.


00:36:19.566 --> 00:36:20.545
What?


00:36:21.835 --> 00:36:23.373
Percy, you got your answer!


00:36:23.470 --> 00:36:25.042
All I got were numbers.


00:36:25.139 --> 00:36:26.585
- Yes.
- You'll know...


00:36:26.773 --> 00:36:28.413
When it matters.


00:36:31.611 --> 00:36:33.422
I think we're a little short on drachmas.


00:36:33.513 --> 00:36:34.492
What?


00:36:47.027 --> 00:36:48.439
What do you... think we're...
running here?


00:36:48.529 --> 00:36:49.439
A charity?


00:36:49.530 --> 00:36:51.164
- Get your cheap butts...
- Out!


00:36:51.165 --> 00:36:51.404
- Get your cheap butts...
- Out!


00:37:01.543 --> 00:37:02.614
That was...


00:37:02.811 --> 00:37:04.018
I know.


00:37:04.713 --> 00:37:07.492
Awesome! Can we go again?


00:37:07.683 --> 00:37:09.790
We're definitely not in Florida.


00:37:10.785 --> 00:37:13.325
I think we're in Olympus.


00:37:13.988 --> 00:37:17.269
Hail to you, great Zeus!
Forgive our trespass on Olympus.


00:37:17.459 --> 00:37:20.101
We're seeking transport to Florida.


00:37:20.896 --> 00:37:21.875
Zeus?


00:37:22.531 --> 00:37:23.510
Zeus?


00:37:24.066 --> 00:37:25.045
Zeus?


00:37:25.234 --> 00:37:28.241
Whoa, stop it, stop it, stop it!
This isn't Olympus, okay?


00:37:28.337 --> 00:37:29.977
This is the Capitol building.


00:37:30.072 --> 00:37:32.884
We're in Washington, D.C. Okay?


00:37:35.144 --> 00:37:36.283
It looks like Olympus.


00:37:36.378 --> 00:37:39.294
Right down to the dudes with power
who only care about themselves.


00:37:39.381 --> 00:37:41.260
We need to find a bus station.


00:37:41.350 --> 00:37:43.354
First we need to get some money.


00:37:48.591 --> 00:37:51.006
<i>Hey, there,
valued half-blood account holder!</i>


00:37:51.094 --> 00:37:54.101
<i>Sign up for our new Aphrodite Express
credit card, and you can--</i>


00:37:54.197 --> 00:37:58.240
Can I get four
venti half-caf no-whip lattes?


00:37:58.435 --> 00:38:01.180
And an extra shot of nectar.


00:38:07.477 --> 00:38:08.456
Nectar?


00:38:08.546 --> 00:38:11.358
If you haven't had,
then you haven't lived, buddy.


00:38:17.755 --> 00:38:19.395
Hecatonshire.


00:38:19.590 --> 00:38:20.569
Hey.


00:38:21.692 --> 00:38:23.833
I see you got your hands full.


00:38:26.630 --> 00:38:27.905
Room for cream?


00:38:28.031 --> 00:38:31.106
Nectar. Double shot.


00:38:39.611 --> 00:38:41.217
I've lived.


00:38:42.080 --> 00:38:44.494
This might be the most fun
I've ever had.


00:38:44.683 --> 00:38:45.822
Ever.


00:38:46.018 --> 00:38:49.559
Yeah, anything's gotta be better
than living in the woods, right?


00:38:49.754 --> 00:38:52.237
Living in the woods would have been fine
if you were there.


00:38:52.324 --> 00:38:54.465
Everything's better with a brother.


00:38:55.394 --> 00:38:58.071
You know, technically,
we don't have the same mom.


00:38:58.163 --> 00:39:01.739
So we're still brothers!
I know! How cool is that?


00:39:01.934 --> 00:39:03.312
Arctic.


00:39:05.070 --> 00:39:06.414
It's too sweet, don't you think?


00:39:06.505 --> 00:39:08.818
No, nectar's never too sweet.


00:39:13.412 --> 00:39:14.893
Get off me!


00:39:15.347 --> 00:39:17.158
- Get off me!
- Grover!


00:39:28.428 --> 00:39:29.430
Percy!


00:39:32.365 --> 00:39:34.473
- Damn!
- Was that Chris Rodriguez?


00:39:34.668 --> 00:39:36.411
How did they do that?


00:39:37.804 --> 00:39:41.483
Back at camp, Luke said that
there were other half-bloods who turned.


00:39:41.575 --> 00:39:43.352
What do you mean, "turned"?


00:39:43.944 --> 00:39:45.550
To his side.


00:39:47.448 --> 00:39:48.757
Luke has Grover.


00:39:49.983 --> 00:39:51.658
The Oracle was right.


00:39:51.852 --> 00:39:55.133
Luke is going after the Fleece.
That's why he needs a satyr.


00:39:55.622 --> 00:39:57.262
But what does Luke want
with the Fleece anyway?


00:39:57.357 --> 00:39:58.428
I don't know.


00:39:58.525 --> 00:40:00.700
But if we're gonna get Grover back,
we need to find Luke.


00:40:00.794 --> 00:40:02.707
But we don't know where he is.


00:40:07.101 --> 00:40:09.811
I know someone who does. Come on.


00:40:16.777 --> 00:40:20.252
What, are we shipping ourselves
overnight express to the Sea of Monsters?


00:40:20.348 --> 00:40:23.491
You want to find Luke?
His dad will know where he is.


00:40:30.525 --> 00:40:33.168
Olympic Parcel Service. Come on.


00:40:33.361 --> 00:40:34.706
Like it? He'll love it.


00:40:34.797 --> 00:40:38.475
Yes, Hephaestus does do quality work.
Everyone else these days, hacks.


00:40:38.567 --> 00:40:40.275
Excuse me, we're looking for Hermes.


00:40:40.368 --> 00:40:43.318
I'm sorry to be the god of obviousness,
but I'm with a customer.


00:40:43.405 --> 00:40:47.050
You want an overnight shipment to Hades,
that will be 250 drachmas.


00:40:47.676 --> 00:40:49.715
Perfect. Thank you, sweetness.


00:40:49.912 --> 00:40:53.260
I will take care of that for you,
and I'll see you next week.


00:40:53.649 --> 00:40:55.358
Now, you.


00:40:55.551 --> 00:40:57.122
You are here about Hermes?


00:40:57.219 --> 00:40:59.098
His son, actually.
It's kind of important.


00:40:59.187 --> 00:41:02.000
Yeah, I could tell the way you burst in here,
all rude-like.


00:41:02.090 --> 00:41:04.164
His son's name is Luke Castellan.


00:41:07.196 --> 00:41:10.737
What has that wayward boy of mine
gotten himself into now?


00:41:11.268 --> 00:41:13.079
Wait, you're...


00:41:13.170 --> 00:41:14.172
Hermes.


00:41:14.371 --> 00:41:16.580
Little insulted
you didn't recognize me.


00:41:16.673 --> 00:41:19.988
My feelings might have even been hurt
if I wasn't such a self-confident individual.


00:41:20.077 --> 00:41:22.116
I don't know if you noticed,
but I'm killing these shorts.


00:41:22.212 --> 00:41:23.283
Sir, we're looking for Luke...


00:41:23.380 --> 00:41:25.521
because he attacked Camp Half-Blood
and kidnapped our friend.


00:41:25.615 --> 00:41:28.360
And we really need your help,
and we don't have a lot of time.


00:41:28.452 --> 00:41:31.664
That's really cute,
how you finish each other's sentences.


00:41:32.923 --> 00:41:33.994
Follow.


00:41:35.725 --> 00:41:38.903
You like this tie? I just bought it.
Hermés, of course.


00:41:39.429 --> 00:41:40.500
Check it out.


00:41:40.597 --> 00:41:43.171
State-of-the-art sorting,
processing and packaging facility.


00:41:43.267 --> 00:41:46.012
If you can box it, we can ship it
at the speed of...


00:41:46.103 --> 00:41:47.675
Well, me.


00:41:47.871 --> 00:41:50.946
We have plans to expand next year.
We're finding we have some space issues.


00:41:51.041 --> 00:41:52.818
So picture this, only bigger.


00:41:52.910 --> 00:41:54.015
Don't touch that.


00:41:54.111 --> 00:41:56.184
We're the fastest-growing
Olympian industry.


00:41:56.280 --> 00:41:58.889
It took a while to get up and running,
but Rome wasn't built in a day.


00:41:58.982 --> 00:42:00.291
Trust me, I was there.


00:42:00.384 --> 00:42:02.698
Excuse me, sir,
we're in a bit of a hurry.


00:42:02.788 --> 00:42:04.531
Relax, my friend. Take it slow.


00:42:04.623 --> 00:42:06.901
Come on! Give me a break!


00:42:07.091 --> 00:42:09.768
Easy for you to say, Your Eminence.


00:42:09.961 --> 00:42:13.811
Actually, Martha, it's not easy for him.
He's the god of freaking speed.


00:42:13.899 --> 00:42:18.478
Except he's not the one whose butt
is stuck to a big silver stick forever!


00:42:18.670 --> 00:42:21.153
<i>Hey, guys, what did I say?</i>


00:42:21.340 --> 00:42:24.517
When we meet new people,
protract your S's. it's more dramatic.


00:42:24.609 --> 00:42:26.055
Makes an impression.


00:42:26.678 --> 00:42:29.252
I'm personally insulted.
Snakes don't talk like that.


00:42:29.348 --> 00:42:31.626
It is a stereotype and it's offensive.


00:42:31.750 --> 00:42:34.063
Bad enough some of our relatives
are hanging out with Medusa...


00:42:34.153 --> 00:42:35.326
turning people to stone.


00:42:35.421 --> 00:42:36.400
All right.


00:42:36.488 --> 00:42:38.697
I love your hair.
I wish my hair would do that.


00:42:38.790 --> 00:42:39.998
Yeah, that will happen.


00:42:40.092 --> 00:42:42.506
Why don't you guys
make yourselves useful?


00:42:42.594 --> 00:42:44.873
Demi-Google Luke for me.
These kids are looking for him.


00:42:44.964 --> 00:42:46.706
- Why?
- Do they have a death wish?


00:42:46.798 --> 00:42:48.507
It doesn't matter. Just...


00:42:48.633 --> 00:42:49.738
Didn't even say "please."


00:42:49.836 --> 00:42:52.148
Told you! We should have taken
that job with Hercules.


00:42:52.238 --> 00:42:53.981
They're an acquired taste.


00:42:54.607 --> 00:42:56.384
Luke. I don't know what to do about him.


00:42:56.476 --> 00:42:59.585
I've tried reaching out, but the kid's angry.
He's resentful.


00:42:59.680 --> 00:43:01.388
And he holds a grudge
like nobody's business.


00:43:01.481 --> 00:43:02.985
Just like his mother,
come to think of it.


00:43:03.083 --> 00:43:04.928
Yeah, he's not my biggest fan either.


00:43:05.018 --> 00:43:08.902
If you're gonna cross paths or,
Zeus forbid, swords with him...


00:43:09.089 --> 00:43:13.007
it wouldn't be the worst thing in the world
to have a thing or two to help you out.


00:43:13.093 --> 00:43:15.097
Collector's item, mint condition.


00:43:15.195 --> 00:43:17.678
<i>From Hercules Busts Heads, Season One.</i>


00:43:17.865 --> 00:43:19.345
<i>Hercules Busts Heads?</i>


00:43:19.533 --> 00:43:20.911
Best TV show ever.


00:43:21.034 --> 00:43:23.984
So, of course, cancelled.


00:43:24.605 --> 00:43:26.484
Got this off Deity-Bay.


00:43:26.674 --> 00:43:29.749
You twist the cap off this, you release the
winds from the four corners of the Earth.


00:43:29.843 --> 00:43:31.984
Now, you tell me that isn't cool.


00:43:32.179 --> 00:43:33.751
Whoa! No, not in here!


00:43:34.448 --> 00:43:35.484
Not in here.


00:43:35.583 --> 00:43:38.965
By the gods, George was right.
You do have a death wish.


00:43:39.820 --> 00:43:41.267
Now, you're also...


00:43:42.723 --> 00:43:44.898
You're also gonna want one of these.


00:43:50.732 --> 00:43:52.042
Thanks.


00:43:52.234 --> 00:43:54.147
Mythical box sealer?


00:43:54.336 --> 00:43:57.047
You wound me. Truly, I am wounded.


00:43:57.239 --> 00:44:00.485
I hold in my hands a Matter Eliminator.
Trademark pending.


00:44:00.675 --> 00:44:02.315
Anything you outline with this...


00:44:02.410 --> 00:44:03.549
Not in here.


00:44:04.012 --> 00:44:05.356
...will disappear.


00:44:06.048 --> 00:44:07.426
Gone. Instant hole.


00:44:07.516 --> 00:44:08.792
"Demi-Google Luke," he said.


00:44:08.884 --> 00:44:10.957
Except, how am I supposed to
type without fingers?


00:44:11.053 --> 00:44:12.590
You were supposed to use the mouse!


00:44:12.687 --> 00:44:14.100
I'm a snake. I eat mice.


00:44:14.189 --> 00:44:16.000
All right, thank you.
Have you found Luke?


00:44:16.091 --> 00:44:17.298
Did he just say "thank you"?


00:44:17.392 --> 00:44:18.964
I'm sure it was just a lapse.


00:44:19.061 --> 00:44:20.667
Luke's on a yacht called the Andromeda.


00:44:20.763 --> 00:44:23.177
It's passing by Chesapeake Beach
as we speak.


00:44:23.265 --> 00:44:24.267
Thank you.


00:44:24.366 --> 00:44:26.109
You're so welcome.


00:44:26.201 --> 00:44:27.546
There, you happy?


00:44:28.203 --> 00:44:29.182
Hush.


00:44:30.372 --> 00:44:31.785
Thank you very much.


00:44:31.874 --> 00:44:33.354
Hey, listen...


00:44:36.178 --> 00:44:37.751
If you see Luke...


00:44:37.948 --> 00:44:41.194
please explain to him for me...


00:44:42.252 --> 00:44:45.533
that parents,
we make mistakes sometimes.


00:44:45.922 --> 00:44:48.769
He has every right to be angry at me.


00:44:48.959 --> 00:44:51.442
Just, please tell him
not to be angry with the world.


00:44:51.528 --> 00:44:55.571
I'm not sure if there's anything
that I can say that will change him.


00:44:55.766 --> 00:44:57.007
Tl"!-


00:44:57.634 --> 00:44:59.616
If it's one thing I've learned
in 3000 years...


00:44:59.703 --> 00:45:02.050
it's you can't give up on family.


00:45:09.313 --> 00:45:10.850
Thanks again.


00:45:12.716 --> 00:45:14.254
He'll never make it.


00:45:15.152 --> 00:45:16.257
That's lunch!


00:45:25.429 --> 00:45:27.638
That's it. That's Luke's yacht.


00:45:27.832 --> 00:45:29.404
What do we do? Swim?


00:45:29.601 --> 00:45:31.082
But it's water.


00:45:32.270 --> 00:45:33.751
Dad will help.


00:45:37.776 --> 00:45:38.755
Hey, Dad.


00:45:38.944 --> 00:45:42.087
We're trying to save Camp Half-Blood
and rescue a satyr named Grover.


00:45:42.180 --> 00:45:45.722
And we could really use your help
getting to that ship out there.


00:45:47.252 --> 00:45:48.460
Poseidon?


00:45:49.154 --> 00:45:50.133
Dad?


00:45:50.456 --> 00:45:51.834
It was a nice try, big guy...


00:45:51.924 --> 00:45:54.737
but don't be upset when he doesn't...


00:46:01.334 --> 00:46:02.837
...answer.


00:46:09.508 --> 00:46:11.387
It's a hippocampus.


00:46:23.690 --> 00:46:24.897
Hi, girl.


00:46:26.860 --> 00:46:28.000
Boy-


00:46:31.265 --> 00:46:32.540
Come here.


00:46:36.937 --> 00:46:39.579
Sometimes, you just gotta ask.


00:46:40.240 --> 00:46:42.688
All I've been doing is asking.


00:46:58.225 --> 00:46:59.501
Are you coming?


00:47:00.460 --> 00:47:01.439
Yeah.


00:47:05.132 --> 00:47:06.407
Are you ready?


00:47:06.600 --> 00:47:07.739
Yeah.


00:47:07.935 --> 00:47:09.176
Giddy up!


00:48:15.839 --> 00:48:16.978
Back up!


00:48:17.608 --> 00:48:18.747
Back up.


00:48:29.219 --> 00:48:30.666
Thank you, friend.


00:48:30.988 --> 00:48:32.229
Tyson.


00:48:32.656 --> 00:48:34.467
Come on, buddy. We gotta go.


00:48:39.197 --> 00:48:40.643
You want some sugar?


00:48:50.674 --> 00:48:52.121
- Have you seen it?
- No, man.


00:48:52.210 --> 00:48:53.189
Did he show it to you?


00:48:53.277 --> 00:48:54.484
Wait until you see it.


00:48:54.578 --> 00:48:56.720
It took him long enough to find it.


00:48:59.218 --> 00:49:02.134
<i>That's Chris Rodriguez, Ethan Nakamura,
and Shana Beauregard.</i>


00:49:02.221 --> 00:49:03.826
Luke's been recruiting.


00:49:06.758 --> 00:49:08.603
This is a nice boat.


00:49:08.793 --> 00:49:10.672
How are we gonna find Grover?


00:49:11.430 --> 00:49:14.607
Luke is probably keeping him
below deck somewhere.


00:49:14.800 --> 00:49:16.144
Like, in a brig.


00:49:16.268 --> 00:49:18.614
I don't think yachts have brigs, Percy.


00:49:20.139 --> 00:49:21.551
Follow me.


00:49:26.245 --> 00:49:29.127
Be careful, you guys.
He said keep your distance.


00:49:29.649 --> 00:49:32.291
How much longer are we gonna
be on this boat, anyway?


00:49:32.384 --> 00:49:34.297
Doesn't matter, just watch it.


00:49:44.964 --> 00:49:46.968
It's so time to go.


00:49:47.333 --> 00:49:49.441
Hey. Percy. Percy!


00:49:54.007 --> 00:49:55.716
Tyson, do you have to
make so much noise?


00:49:55.809 --> 00:49:57.118
Sorry!


00:50:13.727 --> 00:50:14.706
Chris?


00:50:14.795 --> 00:50:15.935
Hey.


00:50:16.297 --> 00:50:18.245
What have you done with Grover?


00:50:18.865 --> 00:50:20.175
Grover?


00:50:20.667 --> 00:50:22.808
Grover's the least of your worries.


00:50:24.605 --> 00:50:25.950
<i>Guess who's here.</i>


00:50:34.982 --> 00:50:38.592
What a surprise.
If it isn't my two favorite cousins.


00:50:38.786 --> 00:50:39.960
Three.


00:50:40.155 --> 00:50:41.932
I'm a son of Poseidon, too.


00:50:42.625 --> 00:50:46.405
That's funny, because Poseidon
doesn't have any other half-blood sons.


00:50:46.528 --> 00:50:48.270
I'm a Cyclops.


00:50:50.866 --> 00:50:51.937
Mist.


00:50:52.134 --> 00:50:53.774
You don't say.


00:50:57.706 --> 00:50:59.483
It's been a long time.


00:51:01.143 --> 00:51:03.022
You look good.


00:51:04.547 --> 00:51:05.891
Where's Grover?


00:51:06.081 --> 00:51:07.858
Grover, Grover.


00:51:08.050 --> 00:51:10.294
Grover, yes.
Right, the satyr.


00:51:10.486 --> 00:51:12.991
He should be in the Sea of Monsters
right about now.


00:51:13.088 --> 00:51:16.665
I sent him on ahead with some friends.
We're kind of on the clock.


00:51:17.326 --> 00:51:18.738
Wait, you're not...


00:51:19.228 --> 00:51:22.110
You're not just trying to stop us
from getting the Fleece.


00:51:22.198 --> 00:51:23.644
I need it, too.


00:51:25.201 --> 00:51:28.014
I got something
only the Fleece can revive.


00:51:28.204 --> 00:51:30.083
And it's not a tree.


00:51:32.209 --> 00:51:33.518
Wanna see it?


00:51:37.882 --> 00:51:40.160
It wasn't easy to find.


00:51:40.517 --> 00:51:43.660
I had to crawl through
the depths of Tartarus itself.


00:51:44.554 --> 00:51:46.593
And then Cleveland.


00:51:47.424 --> 00:51:49.703
The remains of Kronos.


00:51:49.894 --> 00:51:52.901
The original Titan,
father to the Olympians.


00:51:53.097 --> 00:51:56.674
And with the Fleece's help,
destroyer of Olympus.


00:51:56.867 --> 00:51:58.347
And the world.


00:51:58.969 --> 00:52:02.682
You'd destroy the whole world
just to get back at your dad?


00:52:03.173 --> 00:52:05.713
The Olympians overthrew their parents.


00:52:06.243 --> 00:52:07.849
It's just our turn.


00:52:08.178 --> 00:52:09.625
We met your father.


00:52:09.980 --> 00:52:12.896
He said that he knows
that he made mistakes.


00:52:13.083 --> 00:52:15.726
He told us to tell you
to not be so angry.


00:52:16.120 --> 00:52:17.099
Really?


00:52:19.056 --> 00:52:21.300
And he couldn't even tell me himself.


00:52:21.959 --> 00:52:23.669
Does that sound familiar?


00:52:25.264 --> 00:52:26.835
Take them to the brig.


00:52:26.932 --> 00:52:28.242
Let's go. Come on.


00:52:28.334 --> 00:52:31.477
Thalia was your friend!
She sacrificed herself for you.


00:52:32.271 --> 00:52:36.587
You're gonna lecture me about Thalia
when you're hanging around with him?


00:52:38.144 --> 00:52:40.456
You disappoint me the most.


00:53:15.181 --> 00:53:18.324
I told you he had a brig.


00:53:23.891 --> 00:53:25.235
How can you trust him?


00:53:25.325 --> 00:53:26.965
He was probably making all that noise
on purpose.


00:53:27.060 --> 00:53:28.837
He wanted Luke to catch us.


00:53:29.029 --> 00:53:31.307
What do you have against Tyson anyway?


00:53:31.398 --> 00:53:33.003
He's a Cyclops.


00:53:33.200 --> 00:53:36.082
I think the politically correct term
is "ocularly impaired."


00:53:36.169 --> 00:53:38.948
Who cares?
They're vicious and they're dangerous.


00:53:44.812 --> 00:53:47.159
Yeah, vicious.


00:54:07.169 --> 00:54:09.151
We have to get out of here.


00:54:09.338 --> 00:54:10.750
How?


00:54:16.779 --> 00:54:18.761
Just hang on to something.


00:54:49.778 --> 00:54:51.555
All right, here we go.


00:54:55.518 --> 00:54:57.227
Come on, come on, come on!


00:55:07.264 --> 00:55:08.608
What's going on?


00:55:13.970 --> 00:55:15.849
Percy's trying to kill us.


00:55:18.042 --> 00:55:19.545
I think it's working.


00:55:31.621 --> 00:55:32.726
You got it?


00:55:32.923 --> 00:55:34.927
Piece of cake.


00:55:35.126 --> 00:55:37.130
I think I'm gonna vomit.


00:55:37.762 --> 00:55:38.741
Yep.


00:55:40.397 --> 00:55:42.379
So, how does this work?


00:55:42.566 --> 00:55:46.211
I don't know.
It's my first mythical tape gun.


00:56:05.391 --> 00:56:07.464
Just like Hermes said...


00:56:08.260 --> 00:56:09.536
"instant hole."


00:56:39.592 --> 00:56:41.097
Go to the lifeboat.


00:56:51.338 --> 00:56:53.047
Kill the engines.


00:56:58.578 --> 00:57:00.560
That was for Grover.


00:57:11.124 --> 00:57:12.605
Grab him!


00:57:36.285 --> 00:57:37.629
We got him!


00:57:46.195 --> 00:57:47.641
What are you doing?


00:57:48.230 --> 00:57:49.801
Don't walk on my roof.


00:57:55.637 --> 00:57:57.277
Join me, Percy.


00:57:57.472 --> 00:58:01.151
It's what you were meant to do.
You can't escape that prophecy.


00:58:02.078 --> 00:58:04.060
Let's show both of our fathers.


00:58:04.646 --> 00:58:06.059
It's tempting.


00:58:10.586 --> 00:58:13.035
That's genius. Really.


00:58:13.756 --> 00:58:15.327
But I think I'll pass.


00:58:32.075 --> 00:58:33.681
Not this again.


00:58:36.146 --> 00:58:37.125
Go!


00:58:37.213 --> 00:58:39.719
- Are you staying?
- I'll be right behind you.


00:58:43.954 --> 00:58:45.264
May as well.


00:59:19.992 --> 00:59:21.404
Jackson, enough.


00:59:25.998 --> 00:59:28.207
You're on the losing side.


00:59:28.901 --> 00:59:30.609
Not from where I stand.


00:59:48.654 --> 00:59:50.157
Smart.


00:59:50.355 --> 00:59:53.100
Goddess of wisdom's daughter, remember?


00:59:53.959 --> 00:59:55.565
I remember.


01:00:03.803 --> 01:00:07.688
Our allies and the satyr still have
a head start on the Fleece.


01:00:09.310 --> 01:00:11.690
We will resurrect you, Lord Kronos.


01:00:12.446 --> 01:00:14.485
You will know vengeance.


01:00:15.782 --> 01:00:19.256
And the Olympians who scorned us
will know death.


01:00:38.405 --> 01:00:40.820
Maybe you should reapply.


01:00:43.210 --> 01:00:44.519
It wore off?


01:00:46.080 --> 01:00:47.059
Yeah.


01:01:00.328 --> 01:01:01.536
Come on.


01:01:03.365 --> 01:01:04.641
Oh, no.


01:01:10.373 --> 01:01:11.375
Hey.


01:01:12.240 --> 01:01:14.314
Do you want to steer for a while?


01:01:16.545 --> 01:01:17.854
Thank you.


01:01:19.315 --> 01:01:21.820
Nobody's ever trusted me
with anything before.


01:01:21.917 --> 01:01:24.901
Is that because of
your lack of depth perception?


01:01:26.289 --> 01:01:28.464
Is it because they're scared of you?


01:01:32.461 --> 01:01:34.568
I was in the mountains one day...


01:01:35.297 --> 01:01:40.308
and some campers,
Boy Scouts, showed up.


01:01:43.072 --> 01:01:46.716
And when they saw me, they screamed.


01:01:48.277 --> 01:01:49.757
They ran.


01:01:51.481 --> 01:01:53.794
And I'm pretty sure I smiled.


01:01:56.586 --> 01:01:59.468
People look at me,
and they see a monster.


01:02:00.190 --> 01:02:02.536
Sometimes, I think maybe they're right.


01:02:05.162 --> 01:02:08.807
You're not a monster.
Don't be so hard on yourself.


01:02:11.268 --> 01:02:12.749
Easy for you to say.


01:02:12.937 --> 01:02:14.246
What do you mean?


01:02:14.338 --> 01:02:17.687
You never doubt yourself
or think you're less than you are.


01:02:21.679 --> 01:02:23.786
Thank you, brother.


01:02:24.314 --> 01:02:27.025
Come here. Open it slowly.


01:02:27.217 --> 01:02:28.425
Slowly.


01:02:30.288 --> 01:02:34.263
Hey, just take it slow. Slow, okay?


01:02:40.498 --> 01:02:43.381
I wouldn't have trusted him
with a normal thermos.


01:02:43.835 --> 01:02:45.783
He seems okay.


01:02:45.970 --> 01:02:48.749
I really don't get
what your problem with him is.


01:02:51.510 --> 01:02:54.119
Because you don't know
what I know about them.


01:02:54.680 --> 01:02:55.785
Thalia!


01:03:03.389 --> 01:03:05.667
A Cyclops killed her.


01:03:06.993 --> 01:03:09.305
His kind killed Thalia.


01:03:10.830 --> 01:03:12.310
I'm sorry.


01:03:13.733 --> 01:03:15.213
I never knew.


01:03:15.401 --> 01:03:17.975
Well, it's not something
I like talking about.


01:03:19.105 --> 01:03:21.714
And anyway, it was a long time ago.


01:03:31.551 --> 01:03:32.895
What is that?


01:03:34.087 --> 01:03:35.830
It's the Sea of Monsters.


01:03:42.262 --> 01:03:43.834
Why are we stopping?


01:03:47.468 --> 01:03:49.347
I should have used two hands.


01:03:49.437 --> 01:03:50.781
You think?


01:03:51.805 --> 01:03:53.114
Are you mad at me?


01:03:53.207 --> 01:03:55.119
No, not at you.


01:04:12.326 --> 01:04:14.137
Tell me those aren't sharks.


01:04:17.298 --> 01:04:18.973
Those aren't sharks.


01:04:19.901 --> 01:04:22.042
Paddle! Paddle!


01:04:27.142 --> 01:04:29.021
Yeah, sharks would be better.


01:04:43.593 --> 01:04:45.403
It's Charybdis.


01:04:45.595 --> 01:04:46.870
Charyb-... What?


01:04:46.962 --> 01:04:48.944
She guards the Sea of Monsters.


01:04:54.837 --> 01:04:55.976
Percy!


01:05:03.446 --> 01:05:04.983
It's not working!


01:05:05.948 --> 01:05:08.955
The Sea of Monsters
might not be in Poseidon's domain.


01:05:12.522 --> 01:05:13.501
Hold on!


01:05:52.764 --> 01:05:54.301
Where are we?


01:05:56.601 --> 01:05:58.275
Smells like the stomach.


01:06:08.714 --> 01:06:10.593
Watch your step.


01:06:16.755 --> 01:06:18.395
What is this stuff?


01:06:19.191 --> 01:06:21.173
I don't think you want to know.


01:06:22.093 --> 01:06:24.576
This has to be the worst way to die, ever.


01:06:24.763 --> 01:06:28.510
Yeah, everything that disappears
in the Bermuda Triangle...


01:06:28.700 --> 01:06:30.773
this is where they end up.


01:06:31.637 --> 01:06:33.118
Come on!


01:06:34.107 --> 01:06:35.553
That sounded like Clarissa.


01:06:35.641 --> 01:06:37.418
No, it couldn't be her.


01:06:37.610 --> 01:06:40.389
You ridiculously stupid morons.


01:06:40.579 --> 01:06:42.458
- No, it's her.
-It's her.


01:06:47.053 --> 01:06:48.032
You idiot!


01:06:48.121 --> 01:06:51.401
Better keep my electric grid up
and running, or I'll plug your head into it!


01:06:51.490 --> 01:06:53.403
Clarissa! Hey!


01:06:56.229 --> 01:06:59.270
Jackson? What are you doing here?


01:06:59.465 --> 01:07:01.573
We got swallowed up, just like you.


01:07:01.769 --> 01:07:02.840
Nice ship.


01:07:02.937 --> 01:07:06.046
My dad's got tons of this stuff
left over from wars throughout history.


01:07:06.140 --> 01:07:10.616
It was either this or a Huey from Vietnam.
I figured a boat would be more practical.


01:07:13.180 --> 01:07:14.489
What's going on?


01:07:14.582 --> 01:07:18.032
Pretty much exactly what you think
goes on inside of a stomach.


01:07:31.265 --> 01:07:32.610
You're right.


01:07:32.800 --> 01:07:34.713
That really is the worst way to die.


01:07:34.802 --> 01:07:35.804
Reardon!


01:07:35.903 --> 01:07:38.386
What in Hades is going on with my engine?
Is it ready yet?


01:07:38.473 --> 01:07:41.355
Almost, ma'am. They're working on it.


01:07:41.542 --> 01:07:44.150
Wait, your crew is zombies?


01:07:46.681 --> 01:07:48.390
They prefer "dead Confederate sailors


01:07:48.483 --> 01:07:50.431
whose lives have been given
in tribute to Ares."


01:07:50.518 --> 01:07:52.967
But "zombies" is fine.


01:08:07.802 --> 01:08:10.342
Reardon! Gun! Faster! Now!


01:08:10.539 --> 01:08:12.487
Gun is hot, Cap'n. Locked and loaded.


01:08:12.574 --> 01:08:14.556
Aim it at that meat grinder.


01:08:14.743 --> 01:08:16.987
Wait, wait.
You want to shoot that thing with this?


01:08:17.079 --> 01:08:20.222
Do you have a better idea?
Because now would be the time.


01:08:23.720 --> 01:08:24.995
Hey, Clarissa.


01:08:25.755 --> 01:08:26.791
What?


01:08:26.989 --> 01:08:28.230
Can you steer the ship?


01:08:28.324 --> 01:08:31.137
No. I just finished driver's ed.
Yes, of course, I can steer a ship.


01:08:31.227 --> 01:08:32.640
Well...


01:08:33.095 --> 01:08:34.599
why don't we give her a stomach ache?


01:08:34.697 --> 01:08:36.576
We'll escape through the gut.


01:08:37.166 --> 01:08:39.114
It just might work
if it doesn't kill us first.


01:08:39.201 --> 01:08:41.514
You steer, I'll shoot.


01:08:42.605 --> 01:08:44.245
All hands below deck!


01:08:46.677 --> 01:08:48.386
Good luck, Percy.


01:08:53.284 --> 01:08:55.732
All hands below deck.
This is not a drill!


01:08:55.852 --> 01:08:57.834
Come on, boys. Get in there.


01:09:02.125 --> 01:09:03.731
This is still my quest.


01:09:03.927 --> 01:09:06.171
Do not screw this up for me, Jackson.


01:09:25.816 --> 01:09:27.729
You should watch what you eat.


01:09:43.736 --> 01:09:44.715
Go!


01:09:44.904 --> 01:09:46.475
No kidding, genius.


01:09:58.651 --> 01:10:00.462
I hope this works.


01:10:02.688 --> 01:10:05.068
- Just don't forget.
- Forget what?


01:10:07.594 --> 01:10:09.598
This is all your idea.


01:10:24.610 --> 01:10:25.988
Come on, come on.


01:10:38.792 --> 01:10:40.968
- We did it!
- I did it!


01:10:42.529 --> 01:10:44.670
Listen up. Full power to the screws.


01:10:44.866 --> 01:10:46.210
Hey. are you guys all right?


01:10:46.300 --> 01:10:47.644
That was amazing.


01:10:51.740 --> 01:10:53.311
You have to have faith, right?


01:10:53.407 --> 01:10:55.890
And a cannon. We'll find Grover.


01:10:57.812 --> 01:10:59.224
Where is lchneutae?


01:10:59.313 --> 01:11:00.885
Now you miss lchneutae?


01:11:00.982 --> 01:11:04.023
We ran into Scylla,
that multi-headed Hydra thing.


01:11:04.218 --> 01:11:05.824
He said, "I got this."


01:11:06.020 --> 01:11:07.466
Famous last words.


01:11:07.655 --> 01:11:09.694
We've restored full power, Cap'n.


01:11:10.091 --> 01:11:11.800
- Heading?
- Northwest.


01:11:19.668 --> 01:11:21.307
Are you sure about that?


01:11:21.404 --> 01:11:24.718
Yes, I'm sure about that.
Why, do you have a problem?


01:11:24.907 --> 01:11:26.582
Yeah, you got a problem?


01:11:28.010 --> 01:11:33.694
I think your Confederate warship
is heading to West Palm Beach, Florida.


01:11:34.950 --> 01:11:35.929
What is it?


01:11:36.018 --> 01:11:39.526
I know this sounds insane,
but it's kind of like my dyslexia.


01:11:39.722 --> 01:11:43.902
But instead of being able to read Greek,
I can see map lines.


01:11:44.260 --> 01:11:47.176
30. 31, 75,12.


01:11:48.598 --> 01:11:50.910
Wait, that's the numbers from the--


01:11:51.100 --> 01:11:54.744
From the crazy, eyeless taxi drivers.


01:11:54.938 --> 01:11:56.418
They're coordinates.


01:11:56.873 --> 01:11:58.319
Waterboy figured it out.


01:11:58.408 --> 01:11:59.547
And he called you crazy.


01:11:59.642 --> 01:12:00.816
Actually, he called you crazy.


01:12:00.910 --> 01:12:02.720
Hey, eye on the road.


01:12:03.279 --> 01:12:05.352
30, 31 degrees north...


01:12:05.915 --> 01:12:08.022
75,12 degrees west.


01:12:08.218 --> 01:12:10.667
That's where
Polyphemus and the Fleece are.


01:12:10.755 --> 01:12:13.101
Change course. Southwest.


01:12:13.290 --> 01:12:14.635
AVE. aye.


01:12:14.992 --> 01:12:16.233
Sorry.


01:12:39.083 --> 01:12:40.564
Land ho!


01:12:44.322 --> 01:12:46.964
Polyphemus lives in an amusement park?


01:12:47.157 --> 01:12:48.934
No, he lives on an island.


01:12:49.126 --> 01:12:50.607
But the goddess Circe thought building


01:12:50.695 --> 01:12:53.201
an amusement park on top of it
was a good idea.


01:12:53.298 --> 01:12:54.539
It really wasn't.


01:12:54.632 --> 01:12:55.873
What happened?


01:12:56.468 --> 01:12:57.709
Opening day...


01:12:57.802 --> 01:13:01.983
long lines of savory half-bloods
and one hungry Cyclops.


01:13:02.808 --> 01:13:04.187
Bad for business.


01:13:04.943 --> 01:13:06.754
I'll just turn us right around then.


01:13:06.845 --> 01:13:08.758
Find us a place to dock.


01:13:10.016 --> 01:13:12.191
I was afraid she was gonna say that.


01:13:30.970 --> 01:13:33.954
I guess the Cyclops
was bad for business.


01:13:34.140 --> 01:13:35.347
Who knew?


01:13:37.476 --> 01:13:40.358
We don't have time
to search this whole place.


01:13:42.715 --> 01:13:44.389
I don't think we have to.


01:13:46.819 --> 01:13:49.028
"Plummet of Death"?


01:13:49.822 --> 01:13:51.302
That's subtle.


01:13:52.091 --> 01:13:55.099
It looks like something
really big went through there.


01:13:56.330 --> 01:13:59.371
I don't know.
It doesn't really scream "Cyclops" to me.


01:14:03.604 --> 01:14:05.449
At least there's no line.


01:14:11.345 --> 01:14:12.916
Sweet ride.


01:14:16.016 --> 01:14:17.395
Might need a push.


01:14:24.292 --> 01:14:25.795
Here we go.


01:14:27.929 --> 01:14:30.036
Tyson? Let go of my hand.


01:14:30.231 --> 01:14:31.370
Sorry.


01:14:33.835 --> 01:14:37.581
<i>It's a small world after all</i>


01:14:37.772 --> 01:14:41.222
<i>It's a small world after all</i>


01:14:41.409 --> 01:14:43.756
Could you two just shut up?


01:14:47.850 --> 01:14:48.829
Hold on!


01:14:51.353 --> 01:14:52.698
Is everybody okay?


01:14:52.788 --> 01:14:54.861
I thought that would be more fun.


01:15:00.429 --> 01:15:03.140
I think I get what Grover
was so worried about.


01:15:04.801 --> 01:15:07.113
This must be the boulder
Polyphemus used to trap Odysseus...


01:15:07.203 --> 01:15:09.743
when he was returning
from the Trojan War.


01:15:10.340 --> 01:15:12.515
Yeah, that's right. I know stuff.


01:15:28.491 --> 01:15:29.698
Grover!


01:15:31.961 --> 01:15:33.499
Enough!


01:15:35.198 --> 01:15:37.306
I can't take this anymore.


01:15:45.643 --> 01:15:47.056
It's been two days!


01:15:47.145 --> 01:15:49.491
Calm your temper!
Calm your temper!


01:15:50.347 --> 01:15:53.958
I haven't had a decent meal
since those half-bloods you brought!


01:15:54.152 --> 01:15:56.897
And this stupid fleece
is supposed to lure satyrs!


01:15:56.988 --> 01:15:59.095
Do you see any satyrs around here?


01:16:00.491 --> 01:16:03.441
This hunger is making my eyesight worse.


01:16:03.628 --> 01:16:05.336
I could just eat you.


01:16:07.699 --> 01:16:10.443
If you weren't a Cyclops.


01:16:12.670 --> 01:16:13.649
Grover!


01:16:14.972 --> 01:16:15.951
Grover!


01:16:16.474 --> 01:16:17.545
- Hey!
- Come here!


01:16:17.642 --> 01:16:18.621
Percy?


01:16:21.178 --> 01:16:22.157
Hey!


01:16:24.048 --> 01:16:25.791
Why are you wearing a dress?


01:16:25.883 --> 01:16:28.161
I'm having a really bad day!


01:16:28.354 --> 01:16:30.700
Hey, hey, hey!
Do not let that go viral!


01:16:30.890 --> 01:16:33.305
Sorry, there's no way the other kids
would believe me otherwise.


01:16:33.392 --> 01:16:34.804
This is a disguise.


01:16:34.893 --> 01:16:37.467
The guy's half-blind.
He thinks I'm a Cyclops chambermaid.


01:16:37.563 --> 01:16:39.100
I'm showing mad survival skills, here.


01:16:39.199 --> 01:16:40.611
And not a small amount of leg.


01:16:40.700 --> 01:16:41.679
Funny.


01:16:41.767 --> 01:16:45.241
I was trying to stay uneaten long enough to
figure out how to get the Fleece off of him.


01:16:45.338 --> 01:16:46.716
So, did you?


01:16:47.440 --> 01:16:49.820
Do you think I'd still be
dressed like this if I did?


01:16:49.909 --> 01:16:51.549
It's a good look.


01:16:51.744 --> 01:16:52.746
Thanks, Tyson.


01:16:54.614 --> 01:16:59.968
Clopsies, how about I cook you
something to drink...


01:17:00.153 --> 01:17:02.032
to calm your nerves?


01:17:04.090 --> 01:17:06.163
I don't know what to do anymore.


01:17:06.993 --> 01:17:08.302
Go! Go!


01:17:08.494 --> 01:17:11.239
This fleece used to lure satyrs
every day.


01:17:14.100 --> 01:17:17.847
Now things are so bad,
I even had to eat my own sheep.


01:17:18.604 --> 01:17:20.052
The whole flock!


01:17:21.241 --> 01:17:22.950
They were tender, though.


01:17:24.444 --> 01:17:27.485
Drop me, and I promise
you'll never hear the end of it.


01:17:30.551 --> 01:17:32.156
Do you smell something?


01:17:32.520 --> 01:17:34.763
Smells like half-bloods!


01:17:39.960 --> 01:17:40.962
Half-bloods!


01:17:41.061 --> 01:17:42.838
- Get up, quick!
- I was right!


01:17:42.930 --> 01:17:44.434
You stay right there!


01:17:44.532 --> 01:17:46.206
Woman, get a fire going!


01:17:46.401 --> 01:17:47.676
That's not good!


01:17:47.769 --> 01:17:49.215
On second thought...


01:17:49.937 --> 01:17:51.885
I'll just eat you raw!


01:17:52.072 --> 01:17:53.051
Hey!


01:17:55.277 --> 01:17:56.757
Hiya!


01:17:56.944 --> 01:17:58.823
My name's Tyson. How are you?


01:17:59.214 --> 01:18:01.024
These guys are my friends...


01:18:01.316 --> 01:18:03.161
so I was hoping, maybe, we could talk.


01:18:03.251 --> 01:18:05.631
You know, Cyclops to Cyclops.


01:18:05.820 --> 01:18:07.733
You pissant with one eye!


01:18:07.922 --> 01:18:09.426
Hey! Not nice!


01:18:09.624 --> 01:18:11.401
You're no Cyclops!


01:18:11.593 --> 01:18:13.905
You're a traitor to your kind!


01:18:14.096 --> 01:18:15.371
To be honest...


01:18:16.565 --> 01:18:17.704
Huh? What?


01:18:18.634 --> 01:18:19.842
He's my kind.


01:18:19.936 --> 01:18:21.884
You disgust me.


01:18:27.310 --> 01:18:28.654
Going somewhere?


01:18:33.115 --> 01:18:35.792
I think you've got something of mine.


01:18:36.786 --> 01:18:37.959
Annabeth!


01:18:43.359 --> 01:18:44.567
Clarissa!


01:18:56.373 --> 01:18:58.149
Get back here, you punk!


01:18:58.341 --> 01:18:59.753
Yo, Clopsies!


01:19:01.845 --> 01:19:03.521
'Quit!


01:19:04.515 --> 01:19:06.690
Wait, you're a dude?


01:19:06.884 --> 01:19:08.593
Well, that explains a lot.


01:19:08.986 --> 01:19:11.435
-say goodbye.
.Okay. Goodbye!


01:19:11.622 --> 01:19:14.834
You deceitful little brats!
I'll tear off your flesh!


01:19:15.326 --> 01:19:17.433
Come on! Go, go!


01:19:18.129 --> 01:19:19.632
Give me that fleece!


01:19:29.140 --> 01:19:30.279
You're dead!


01:19:30.408 --> 01:19:32.117
I'm gonna kill all of you!


01:19:32.476 --> 01:19:34.321
Do you hear me?


01:19:37.748 --> 01:19:39.388
Get back here!


01:19:45.656 --> 01:19:47.103
We rocked that quest.


01:19:47.191 --> 01:19:48.831
Yeah, we totally did.


01:19:49.027 --> 01:19:51.270
I didn't know you guys had it in you!


01:19:51.596 --> 01:19:52.668
Yes.


01:19:53.098 --> 01:19:54.373
Well done.


01:19:58.203 --> 01:20:00.550
It's nice work. I really appreciate it.


01:20:02.308 --> 01:20:03.584
I'll take that.


01:20:07.413 --> 01:20:08.758
I don't think so.


01:20:10.450 --> 01:20:11.691
Suit yourself.


01:20:28.834 --> 01:20:30.543
You'd do it for me.


01:20:32.105 --> 01:20:33.312
No!


01:20:57.464 --> 01:20:59.446
Just remember...


01:20:59.633 --> 01:21:01.637
it didn't have to end this way.


01:21:03.004 --> 01:21:04.849
This one's on you.


01:21:11.279 --> 01:21:12.589
Down, boy!


01:21:20.021 --> 01:21:22.264
You should consider yourselves lucky.


01:21:22.857 --> 01:21:25.169
This has been millennia in the making.


01:21:25.994 --> 01:21:27.771
And you all get to see it.


01:21:28.397 --> 01:21:30.379
You used to be one of us!


01:21:32.200 --> 01:21:33.840
And then I woke up.


01:21:38.507 --> 01:21:42.186
Percy, if Kronos comes back, that's it.
Game over.


01:21:44.347 --> 01:21:45.622
Percy.


01:21:47.183 --> 01:21:49.061
I never called him "brother."


01:21:51.087 --> 01:21:53.501
All he ever wanted was a brother...


01:21:54.824 --> 01:21:57.398
but I was too wrapped up in myself.


01:21:59.329 --> 01:22:01.972
And now Luke has the Fleece...


01:22:02.165 --> 01:22:04.306
because I gave it to him.


01:22:06.002 --> 01:22:10.216
I destroy Olympus,
just like the Oracle said.


01:22:12.241 --> 01:22:13.619
Forget the Oracle.


01:22:15.278 --> 01:22:18.387
You're worried about your destiny?
Then write a new one.


01:22:19.448 --> 01:22:23.457
You're angry at Poseidon for ignoring you?
Then show him why he shouldn't.


01:22:23.987 --> 01:22:25.969
You're upset about Tyson?


01:22:27.591 --> 01:22:29.573
Then make sure
he didn't die for nothing.


01:22:29.660 --> 01:22:31.369
She's right.


01:22:33.898 --> 01:22:35.037
What?


01:22:35.232 --> 01:22:37.943
There's no way
you're getting me to repeat that.


01:22:39.471 --> 01:22:41.510
What Annabeth is saying, Perce...


01:22:41.606 --> 01:22:43.884
is that we're with you.


01:22:44.074 --> 01:22:45.783
Just give the word.


01:22:46.176 --> 01:22:47.589
Why me?


01:22:48.178 --> 01:22:49.989
I mean, who voted me leader?


01:23:03.761 --> 01:23:07.679
Lord Kronos,
he who was betrayed by his sons...


01:23:07.865 --> 01:23:10.781
hear now the words
of one betrayed by his father.


01:23:10.968 --> 01:23:13.577
I bid you... rise.


01:23:52.311 --> 01:23:53.290
Grover!


01:23:55.081 --> 01:23:56.060
Hands.


01:23:56.550 --> 01:23:59.796
Try not to cut them off.
I'm pretty attached to them.


01:24:19.207 --> 01:24:21.120
I have to get to the Fleece.


01:24:21.309 --> 01:24:23.291
So, what are we supposed to do?


01:24:25.246 --> 01:24:26.624
Right.


01:24:55.209 --> 01:24:57.715
I know you can breathe under water,
Jackson.


01:24:57.846 --> 01:24:59.759
But can you breathe like this?


01:25:10.259 --> 01:25:11.398
Hi, Brother!


01:25:24.974 --> 01:25:26.010
What the--?


01:25:26.108 --> 01:25:27.282
The water.


01:25:28.811 --> 01:25:30.258
It healed me.


01:25:32.382 --> 01:25:34.227
Son of Poseidon.


01:25:39.122 --> 01:25:40.397
Thank you...


01:25:42.092 --> 01:25:43.470
Brother.


01:26:07.485 --> 01:26:08.795
He rises.


01:26:26.137 --> 01:26:27.412
Master!


01:26:27.605 --> 01:26:29.210
I brought you back!


01:26:38.350 --> 01:26:40.126
My Lord!


01:26:40.318 --> 01:26:41.389
It's Luke!


01:26:41.953 --> 01:26:43.457
Luke Castellan!


01:26:44.188 --> 01:26:46.296
Your great-grandson!


01:26:47.525 --> 01:26:49.131
My favorite.


01:27:35.975 --> 01:27:37.148
Grover!


01:28:12.580 --> 01:28:14.459
It's the cursed blade!


01:28:16.151 --> 01:28:18.030
"...cursed blade shall reap."


01:28:45.247 --> 01:28:47.696
You want to know
who gave me this sword?


01:28:48.785 --> 01:28:51.792
The god that killed you with it
in the first place!


01:28:55.091 --> 01:28:56.435
My father.


01:28:57.594 --> 01:28:59.131
Percy Jackson...


01:28:59.328 --> 01:29:01.937
your destiny was written long ago.


01:29:04.300 --> 01:29:05.372
No!


01:29:08.605 --> 01:29:10.746
I make my own destiny.


01:29:47.345 --> 01:29:48.518
Half-blood!


01:29:49.480 --> 01:29:51.861
Just in time for dinner.


01:30:16.642 --> 01:30:17.849
Thanks, Dad.


01:30:20.480 --> 01:30:21.789
Percy.


01:30:29.555 --> 01:30:30.899
Annabeth!


01:30:34.427 --> 01:30:35.406
Grover!


01:30:58.785 --> 01:30:59.925
Annabeth!


01:31:02.755 --> 01:31:03.997
No, no!


01:31:04.357 --> 01:31:07.001
At least I'll be with Thalia in Elysium.


01:31:07.461 --> 01:31:09.374
Come here. Give me the Fleece!


01:31:09.630 --> 01:31:10.975
Come on! Come on.


01:31:11.132 --> 01:31:12.111
Come on.


01:31:14.301 --> 01:31:18.219
We make our own destinies, right?
So show me.


01:31:18.406 --> 01:31:19.887
I have faith in you.


01:31:23.444 --> 01:31:26.291
No, no. Come on, show me.


01:31:27.214 --> 01:31:28.455
Show me.


01:31:30.118 --> 01:31:31.427
Come on.


01:32:07.123 --> 01:32:08.159
Annie.


01:32:13.696 --> 01:32:15.006
What happened?


01:32:15.798 --> 01:32:16.904
Don't worry about it.


01:32:17.000 --> 01:32:19.414
If anyone else wants to die tonight...


01:32:19.602 --> 01:32:21.641
at least we have this.


01:32:23.272 --> 01:32:25.652
Hey. You're alive.


01:32:26.509 --> 01:32:27.922
Yeah.


01:32:28.678 --> 01:32:30.991
What you did for Percy...


01:32:32.548 --> 01:32:34.827
that was not so vicious and dangerous.


01:32:37.153 --> 01:32:38.634
Thanks.


01:32:39.389 --> 01:32:40.368
No.


01:32:41.024 --> 01:32:42.299
Thank you.


01:32:53.538 --> 01:32:54.517
You know what, Tyson?


01:32:54.605 --> 01:32:57.281
I know a lot of campers with two eyes
who couldn't do what you did.


01:32:57.375 --> 01:32:59.414
- Hey, Clarissa.
- What?


01:32:59.611 --> 01:33:02.025
Come on, big guy.
We get back to camp, the nectar's on me.


01:33:02.112 --> 01:33:03.787
Have you met the nymphs?


01:33:04.516 --> 01:33:05.996
This was your quest.


01:33:07.051 --> 01:33:10.662
I couldn't have done it without you.


01:33:10.855 --> 01:33:13.064
I think you should
be the one who gets to...


01:33:13.158 --> 01:33:14.832
...do the honors.


01:33:31.176 --> 01:33:33.283
Here you go, Thalia.


01:34:46.187 --> 01:34:49.763
Clarissa! Clarissa! Clarissa!


01:34:55.396 --> 01:34:56.671
Nectar?


01:34:58.666 --> 01:34:59.702
If you haven't had...


01:34:59.801 --> 01:35:01.304
...you haven't lived.


01:35:06.507 --> 01:35:07.749
You know what?


01:35:09.143 --> 01:35:11.182
You don't need these anymore.


01:35:12.814 --> 01:35:14.317
There, that's better.


01:35:28.865 --> 01:35:30.140
<i>You seem happy.</i>


01:35:30.666 --> 01:35:34.379
I'm just relieved to have that whole
prophecy thing off my shoulders.


01:35:34.570 --> 01:35:37.178
I'm not altogether sure it is, Percy.


01:35:37.373 --> 01:35:41.450
You've done wonderfully, but you are
still the only living human child...


01:35:41.644 --> 01:35:43.922
of Poseidon, Hades, or Zeus.


01:35:44.113 --> 01:35:45.526
Besides...


01:35:45.715 --> 01:35:47.993
it's quite possible
the Oracle wasn't referring


01:35:48.085 --> 01:35:50.761
to what would unfold
on Polyphemus' island.


01:35:50.953 --> 01:35:53.869
I'm just saying, a lot can happen
between now and your 20th birthday.


01:35:53.956 --> 01:35:55.938
That's not really what I meant.


01:35:56.059 --> 01:35:59.703
What I meant was
finding out you have a destiny...


01:35:59.896 --> 01:36:03.473
is a lot like finding out you have
a half-brother who's a Cyclops.


01:36:03.867 --> 01:36:06.110
It might not be as bad as you think.


01:36:19.050 --> 01:36:21.659
Percy! Percy!


01:36:22.787 --> 01:36:24.096
Percy!


01:36:24.455 --> 01:36:27.234
Annabeth was guarding the tree
last night...


01:36:27.425 --> 01:36:29.031
and something happened.


01:36:31.195 --> 01:36:32.266
Percy.


01:36:32.897 --> 01:36:34.537
- The Fleece!
- What happened?


01:36:34.633 --> 01:36:37.206
It was even more powerful
than we thought.


01:36:56.921 --> 01:36:58.300
Come on, help her.


01:37:00.124 --> 01:37:01.298
Who are you?


01:37:02.294 --> 01:37:04.640
Percy.
Everything's all right, it's okay.


01:37:05.062 --> 01:37:06.509
I had the strangest dream.


01:37:06.598 --> 01:37:07.577
Yeah?


01:37:07.665 --> 01:37:09.545
Like I was dying.


01:37:09.935 --> 01:37:11.280
What's your name?


01:37:12.405 --> 01:37:15.548
I'm Thalia, daughter of Zeus.


01:37:18.278 --> 01:37:21.262
<i>Another living child of the eldest gods.</i>


01:37:24.117 --> 01:37:26.326
<i>Maybe it wasn't me.</i>


01:37:26.519 --> 01:37:29.332
<i>Maybe the Oracle meant Thalia all along.</i>


01:37:30.790 --> 01:37:33.136
<i>Could she be our salvation?</i>


01:37:33.526 --> 01:37:35.941
<i>Or the cause of our destruction?</i>

